    "title": "Eric Swalwell raises questions on government funding and national security via social media",
    "text": "Rep. Eric Swalwell, a member of the U.S. Congress representing California’s 14th district since 2013, has raised concerns over government funding, law enforcement technology, and FBI transparency in a series of posts on social media.\nOn September 16, 2025, Swalwell questioned government appropriations in light of press freedom issues: “How can we fund this? I am being asked this week to fund a government that locks up a reporter Trump doesn’t like. This isn’t a close call folks.”\nLater that day, he commented on the importance of domestic manufacturing for law enforcement technology: “Drones for law enforcement has changed the game — it is essential that we do what we can to expedite the manufacturing of American made components to ensure national security.”\nOn September 17, 2025, Swalwell questioned FBI procedures related to high-profile investigations: “Why can’t the FBI director answer whether or not he warned Trump that he was in the Epstein files?”\nEric Swalwell has served as a representative from California since succeeding Pete Stark in 2013. Born in Sac City, Iowa in 1980 and currently residing in Livermore, Swalwell holds degrees from the University of Maryland at College Park (BA) and Baltimore (JD).",
